**Architecture**: API Gateway (HTTP endpoint) → Lambda function (Java) → DynamoDB/RDS

```java
// Dependencies (pom.xml)
<dependencies>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>com.amazonaws</groupId>
    <artifactId>aws-lambda-java-core</artifactId>
    <version>1.2.2</version>
  </dependency>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>com.amazonaws</groupId>
    <artifactId>aws-lambda-java-events</artifactId>
    <version>3.11.0</version>
  </dependency>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>com.google.code.gson</groupId>
    <artifactId>gson</artifactId>
    <version>2.10.1</version>
  </dependency>
</dependencies>

// Lambda Handler
public class OrderHandler implements RequestHandler<APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent, APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent> {
  private final Gson gson = new Gson();
  private final DynamoDbClient dynamoDb;

  public OrderHandler() {
    this.dynamoDb = DynamoDbClient.builder()
      .region(Region.US_EAST_1)
      .build();
  }

  @Override
  public APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent handleRequest(
    APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent request,
    Context context
  ) {
    LambdaLogger logger = context.getLogger();
    logger.log("Received request: " + request.getPath());

    try {
      String method = request.getHttpMethod();
      String path = request.getPath();

      // Route requests
      if ("POST".equals(method) && "/orders".equals(path)) {
        return createOrder(request, logger);
      } else if ("GET".equals(method) && path.startsWith("/orders/")) {
        String orderId = extractOrderId(path);
        return getOrder(orderId, logger);
      } else if ("GET".equals(method) && "/orders".equals(path)) {
        return listOrders(request, logger);
      } else {
        return createResponse(404, "{\"error\": \"Not found\"}");
      }
    } catch (Exception e) {
      logger.log("Error: " + e.getMessage());
      return createResponse(500, "{\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}");
    }
  }

  private APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent createOrder(
    APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent request,
    LambdaLogger logger
  ) {
    // Parse request body
    CreateOrderRequest orderRequest = gson.fromJson(
      request.getBody(),
      CreateOrderRequest.class
    );

    // Create order
    String orderId = UUID.randomUUID().toString();
    Order order = new Order(
      orderId,
      orderRequest.getCustomerId(),
      orderRequest.getItems(),
      Instant.now().toString()
    );

    // Save to DynamoDB
    Map<String, AttributeValue> item = new HashMap<>();
    item.put("orderId", AttributeValue.builder().s(orderId).build());
    item.put("customerId", AttributeValue.builder().s(order.getCustomerId()).build());
    item.put("items", AttributeValue.builder().s(gson.toJson(order.getItems())).build());
    item.put("createdAt", AttributeValue.builder().s(order.getCreatedAt()).build());

    PutItemRequest putRequest = PutItemRequest.builder()
      .tableName("Orders")
      .item(item)
      .build();

    dynamoDb.putItem(putRequest);

    logger.log("Created order: " + orderId);

    return createResponse(201, gson.toJson(order));
  }

  private APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent getOrder(String orderId, LambdaLogger logger) {
    // Query DynamoDB
    Map<String, AttributeValue> key = new HashMap<>();
    key.put("orderId", AttributeValue.builder().s(orderId).build());

    GetItemRequest getRequest = GetItemRequest.builder()
      .tableName("Orders")
      .key(key)
      .build();

    GetItemResponse response = dynamoDb.getItem(getRequest);

    if (!response.hasItem()) {
      return createResponse(404, "{\"error\": \"Order not found\"}");
    }

    // Convert to Order object
    Map<String, AttributeValue> item = response.item();
    Order order = new Order(
      item.get("orderId").s(),
      item.get("customerId").s(),
      gson.fromJson(item.get("items").s(), List.class),
      item.get("createdAt").s()
    );

    return createResponse(200, gson.toJson(order));
  }

  private APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent listOrders(
    APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent request,
    LambdaLogger logger
  ) {
    // Get query parameter
    Map<String, String> queryParams = request.getQueryStringParameters();
    String customerId = queryParams != null ? queryParams.get("customerId") : null;

    if (customerId != null) {
      // Query by customer
      Map<String, AttributeValue> expressionValues = new HashMap<>();
      expressionValues.put(":customerId", 
        AttributeValue.builder().s(customerId).build());

      QueryRequest queryRequest = QueryRequest.builder()
        .tableName("Orders")
        .indexName("CustomerIdIndex")
        .keyConditionExpression("customerId = :customerId")
        .expressionAttributeValues(expressionValues)
        .build();

      QueryResponse queryResponse = dynamoDb.query(queryRequest);

      List<Order> orders = queryResponse.items().stream()
        .map(this::convertToOrder)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

      return createResponse(200, gson.toJson(orders));
    } else {
      // Scan all (expensive, use carefully)
      ScanRequest scanRequest = ScanRequest.builder()
        .tableName("Orders")
        .limit(100)
        .build();

      ScanResponse scanResponse = dynamoDb.scan(scanRequest);

      List<Order> orders = scanResponse.items().stream()
        .map(this::convertToOrder)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

      return createResponse(200, gson.toJson(orders));
    }
  }

  private Order convertToOrder(Map<String, AttributeValue> item) {
    return new Order(
      item.get("orderId").s(),
      item.get("customerId").s(),
      gson.fromJson(item.get("items").s(), List.class),
      item.get("createdAt").s()
    );
  }

  private APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent createResponse(int statusCode, String body) {
    Map<String, String> headers = new HashMap<>();
    headers.put("Content-Type", "application/json");
    headers.put("Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "*");

    return new APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent()
      .withStatusCode(statusCode)
      .withHeaders(headers)
      .withBody(body);
  }

  private String extractOrderId(String path) {
    return path.substring(path.lastIndexOf('/') + 1);
  }
}

// Model classes
public class Order {
  private String orderId;
  private String customerId;
  private List<OrderItem> items;
  private String createdAt;

  // Constructor, getters, setters
}

public class CreateOrderRequest {
  private String customerId;
  private List<OrderItem> items;

  // Getters, setters
}
```

**Deployment (AWS SAM)**
```yaml
# template.yaml
AWSTemplateFormatVersion: '2010-09-09'
Transform: AWS::Serverless-2016-10-31

Globals:
  Function:
    Timeout: 30
    MemorySize: 512
    Runtime: java11

Resources:
  OrderFunction:
    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function
    Properties:
      Handler: com.example.OrderHandler::handleRequest
      CodeUri: target/order-lambda-1.0.0.jar
      Environment:
        Variables:
          TABLE_NAME: Orders
      Policies:
        - DynamoDBCrudPolicy:
            TableName: !Ref OrdersTable
      Events:
        CreateOrder:
          Type: Api
          Properties:
            Path: /orders
            Method: POST
        GetOrder:
          Type: Api
          Properties:
            Path: /orders/{orderId}
            Method: GET
        ListOrders:
          Type: Api
          Properties:
            Path: /orders
            Method: GET

  OrdersTable:
    Type: AWS::DynamoDB::Table
    Properties:
      TableName: Orders
      AttributeDefinitions:
        - AttributeName: orderId
          AttributeType: S
        - AttributeName: customerId
          AttributeType: S
      KeySchema:
        - AttributeName: orderId
          KeyType: HASH
      GlobalSecondaryIndexes:
        - IndexName: CustomerIdIndex
          KeySchema:
            - AttributeName: customerId
              KeyType: HASH
          Projection:
            ProjectionType: ALL
          ProvisionedThroughput:
            ReadCapacityUnits: 5
            WriteCapacityUnits: 5
      ProvisionedThroughput:
        ReadCapacityUnits: 5
        WriteCapacityUnits: 5

Outputs:
  ApiUrl:
    Description: "API Gateway endpoint URL"
    Value: !Sub "https://${ServerlessRestApi}.execute-api.${AWS::Region}.amazonaws.com/Prod/"
```

**Build & Deploy**
```bash
# Build
mvn clean package

# Deploy
sam deploy --guided

# Test
curl -X POST https://abc123.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/Prod/orders \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"customerId": "cust123", "items": [{"sku": "SKU001", "quantity": 2}]}'
```

Benefits: No server management, auto-scaling, pay per request, built-in high availability.

Challenges: Cold starts (~1-2s for Java), 15-min timeout, stateless, limited resources (10GB memory max).

**Challenges**

1. **Cold Start**: First invocation loads JVM, initializes classes. Java cold start: 1-3 seconds. Node.js/Python: 100-500ms.
2. **Memory**: JVM heap overhead. Minimum 512MB recommended for Java.
3. **Package Size**: Fat JARs are large (20-50MB). Increases deployment time.
4. **Class Loading**: Java loads classes lazily. First use is slow.

**Optimization Strategies**

**1. Provisioned Concurrency**
```yaml
# template.yaml
Resources:
  OrderFunction:
    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function
    Properties:
      Handler: com.example.OrderHandler
      AutoPublishAlias: live
      ProvisionedConcurrencyConfig:
        ProvisionedConcurrentExecutions: 5 # Keep 5 warm instances

# Or via CLI
aws lambda put-provisioned-concurrency-config \
  --function-name order-function \
  --provisioned-concurrent-executions 5 \
  --qualifier live
```
Benefit: Eliminates cold starts for provisioned instances. Cost: Pay for provisioned capacity.

**2. Minimize Package Size**
```xml
<!-- Use maven-shade-plugin to minimize JAR -->
<plugin>
  <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
  <artifactId>maven-shade-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>3.4.1</version>
  <configuration>
    <createDependencyReducedPom>false</createDependencyReducedPom>
    <minimizeJar>true</minimizeJar> <!-- Remove unused classes -->
    <filters>
      <filter>
        <artifact>*:*</artifact>
        <excludes>
          <exclude>META-INF/*.SF</exclude>
          <exclude>META-INF/*.DSA</exclude>
          <exclude>META-INF/*.RSA</exclude>
        </excludes>
      </filter>
    </filters>
  </configuration>
</plugin>
```

**3. Use Lightweight Frameworks**
```java
// Avoid Spring Boot (heavy)
// Use lightweight alternatives

// Option 1: Plain Lambda (no framework)
public class OrderHandler implements RequestHandler<...> {
  // Direct implementation, fastest cold start
}

// Option 2: Micronaut (AOT compilation)
@Introspected
public class OrderHandler implements MicronautRequestHandler<APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent, APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent> {
  // Micronaut uses AOT, faster startup
}

// Option 3: Quarkus (native compilation)
// Can compile to native binary (GraalVM)
// Cold start: ~50ms (like Python!)
```

**4. Lazy Initialization**
```java
public class OrderHandler implements RequestHandler<...> {
  // Initialize once per container (not per invocation)
  private static final Gson gson = new Gson();
  private static DynamoDbClient dynamoDb;

  static {
    // Static initializer runs during cold start
    dynamoDb = DynamoDbClient.builder()
      .region(Region.US_EAST_1)
      .httpClientBuilder(UrlConnectionHttpClient.builder()) // Lightweight client
      .build();
  }

  // Lazy load heavy dependencies
  private static S3Client s3Client;

  private S3Client getS3Client() {
    if (s3Client == null) {
      s3Client = S3Client.builder().build();
    }
    return s3Client;
  }

  @Override
  public APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent handleRequest(
    APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent request,
    Context context
  ) {
    // Only load S3 if needed
    if (request.getPath().contains("/upload")) {
      S3Client client = getS3Client();
      // Use S3
    }

    // Handle request
  }
}
```

**5. Increase Memory**
```yaml
# More memory = more CPU = faster cold start
Resources:
  OrderFunction:
    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function
    Properties:
      MemorySize: 1024 # 1GB (faster than 512MB)
      # Cost increases linearly, but cold start improves
```
Rule of thumb: 1024MB is sweet spot for Java (2x memory, <2x cost, >2x faster).

**6. Use SnapStart (Java 11+)**
```yaml
# AWS Lambda SnapStart (preview feature)
Resources:
  OrderFunction:
    Type: AWS::Serverless::Function
    Properties:
      Runtime: java11
      SnapStart:
        ApplyOn: PublishedVersions
      # Takes snapshot after initialization
      # Restores from snapshot on cold start
      # Cold start: ~200ms (90% improvement!)
```

**7. Keep Functions Warm**
```java
// CloudWatch Events trigger every 5 minutes
@Override
public APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent handleRequest(
  APIGatewayProxyRequestEvent request,
  Context context
) {
  // Detect warming request
  if ("warming".equals(request.getHeaders().get("X-Warming"))) {
    return new APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent()
      .withStatusCode(200)
      .withBody("{\"warmed\": true}");
  }

  // Normal request handling
  return processRequest(request);
}

// CloudWatch Event rule
{
  "source": ["aws.events"],
  "detail-type": ["Scheduled Event"],
  "schedule": "rate(5 minutes)"
}
```

**8. Profile Cold Start**
```java
public class OrderHandler implements RequestHandler<...> {
  private static final long INIT_START = System.currentTimeMillis();

  static {
    // Heavy initialization
    long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
    initializeDependencies();
    System.out.println("Init time: " + (System.currentTimeMillis() - start) + "ms");
  }

  @Override
  public APIGatewayProxyResponseEvent handleRequest(...) {
    boolean coldStart = System.currentTimeMillis() - INIT_START < 100;

    if (coldStart) {
      System.out.println("COLD START detected");
      // Emit custom metric
      cloudWatchClient.putMetricData(
        PutMetricDataRequest.builder()
          .namespace("Lambda")
          .metricData(MetricDatum.builder()
            .metricName("ColdStart")
            .value(1.0)
            .unit(StandardUnit.COUNT)
            .build())
          .build()
      );
    }

    // Process request
  }
}
```

**9. Use Custom Runtime (GraalVM Native)**
```bash
# Compile to native binary with GraalVM
native-image --no-fallback \
  -jar target/order-lambda.jar \
  -H:Name=bootstrap \
  -H:+ReportExceptionStackTraces

# Package as custom runtime
zip function.zip bootstrap

# Deploy
aws lambda create-function \
  --function-name order-function \
  --runtime provided.al2 \
  --handler bootstrap \
  --zip-file fileb://function.zip

# Result: Cold start ~50ms!
```

**Comparison**

| Approach | Cold Start | Cost | Effort |
|----------|-----------|------|--------|
| Standard Java | 2-3s | Low | Low |
| Optimized JAR | 1-2s | Low | Medium |
| Provisioned Concurrency | ~0ms | High | Low |
| SnapStart | ~200ms | Low | Low |
| GraalVM Native | ~50ms | Low | High |
| Micronaut/Quarkus | ~500ms | Low | Medium |

Recommendation: Start with SnapStart (easiest). If not enough, use GraalVM native (best performance). Provisioned Concurrency for critical APIs (expensive).
